# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, which without this file copies the ENTIRE
# build context into the image: git history, local databases, the developer's
# own résumé — and, on any machine where one exists, .env with live keys, baked
# into a layer. Keep this list in step with .gitignore.

# Secrets — never in an image layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# VCS + tooling
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.DS_Store

# Local data: SQLite DBs, FAISS indexes, generated docs, the master résumé
data/*.db
data/*.faiss
data/*.npy
data/*.png
data/tailored/
data/training/
data/models/
data/resume_master.md
data/resume_master.docx
data/compiler_replay_report.json

# Not needed at runtime. NOTE: no blanket "*.md" — data/profiles/*.md are read
# at runtime by the founder's tailoring path, and scripts/ is imported by the
# admin compiler-replay route, so neither may be excluded.
node_modules
scratch/
tests/
extension-tests/
mobile/
docs/
CLAUDE.md
